    "description": "AdminCredentialClient verifies an administrative challenge through a DeviceSession interface. Its verify method must open a session, write the exact challenge bytes, read a six-byte response, and close the session, in that order and exactly once each. The method exposes only a boolean result to its caller, while the actual device commands and their ordering have no other observable effect. Compliance requires the test to reject an open after write, a missing read, duplicate writes, or failure to close. Hardware is unavailable in the test environment, so the production device cannot be used. Decide how to provide a DeviceSession implementation that permits the client to complete its flow while making every protocol violation immediately visible to the test.",
    "decision_statement": "Whether to use an in-test device implementation that enforces the required command sequence, argument, and cardinality as the client performs them.",
    "notes": "The DeviceSession double enforces command sequence, arguments, and cardinality during the run (mock); spy is the near-miss for asserting the recorded trace after the fact."
